# L §4.3: "An at that is a hole makes the def a hole at those keys, carrying the at's questions, and its rules
# aren't evaluated."  The rule would divide by zero; the at is a hole, so the result is the hole.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input when_d: date
input zero: int
input one: int

def y: num at when_d
  rule base = one / zero

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  when_d = ?"on which day?"
  zero = 0
  one = 1

ask q1: y
=== expect
q1: ?"on which day?" (when_d)
  cut 2026-12-31
